  "reason": "Phase 11d/11e/11f: precision and severity, with the denominator deliberately untouched (callSites identical on all five repos). 11d — no-deep-css-chain measures depth per selector from the tokenizer, so a comma list is no longer a chain (mattermost -4 findings; 'strong em, em strong' scored 3 and is 1). 11e — .nth() moves out of no-nth-child into a new avoid-positional-access rule at warn: 1:1 finding swap (cal.com 113, documenso 126, immich 6, Ghost 2), no count change. 11f — locator('..') moves out of no-xpath into avoid-parent-traversal at info: it was 6 of 8 xpath findings, so the loud rule was mostly reporting the quiet case. Scores rise (cal.com 69->74, immich 89->91, Ghost 98->99, documenso 89->91, mattermost 66->67) entirely from those two deliberate severity reductions, arithmetic checked: cal.com is 113 findings x 3 weight points / (1326 x 5) = 5.1%. Not from the denominator: extracting .first()/.last() would add ~10% more call sites and move every score 3-8 points, enough to flip a --min-score 70 gate, so it is deferred to Phase 12 which owns the denominator.",
